# Kalshi Trading

Standalone Kalshi BTC/ETH prediction market trading system. Independent of any other project — separate Vercel deploy, separate proxy, separate everything.

## Project structure

```
kalshi-trading/
├── api/
│   ├── proxy.js      # CommonJS proxy: Kalshi (public + signed), Polygon, Upstash
│   └── health.js     # Health check endpoint
├── index.html        # Landing page
└── README.md
```

No `package.json`. No `vercel.json`. CommonJS `module.exports` format means zero module-mode configuration needed.

## Required Vercel env variables

|Variable                  |Source                            |Purpose                                    |
|--------------------------|----------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
|`KALSHI_KEY_ID`           |Kalshi dashboard → API Keys       |Identifier for your API key                |
|`KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY`      |Downloaded `.pem` file from Kalshi|Full PEM contents including BEGIN/END lines|
|`POLYGON_API_KEY`         |polygon.io account                |For BTC/ETH price bars                     |
|`UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL`  |upstash.com console               |Redis URL for persistence                  |
|`UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`|upstash.com console               |Redis auth token                           |

## After deploy, verify

Visit `https://your-project.vercel.app/api/health` in a browser. Should see JSON like:

```json
{
  "timestamp": "2026-05-04T...",
  "node": "v20.x",
  "env": {
    "KALSHI_KEY_ID": true,
    "KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY": true,
    "POLYGON_API_KEY": true,
    "UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL": true,
    "UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN": true
  },
  "status": "alive"
}
```

If any env var shows `false`, that variable is missing from Vercel.

## Test Kalshi public endpoint

In browser DevTools console on your deployed site:

```javascript
fetch('/api/proxy', {method:'POST', headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body:JSON.stringify({_kalshi:true, url:'https://api.elections.kalshi.com/trade-api/v2/exchange/status'})}).then(r=>r.json()).then(console.log)
```

Should return `{exchange_active: true, ...}`.

## Test Kalshi signed endpoint

```javascript
fetch('/api/proxy', {method:'POST', headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body:JSON.stringify({_kalshi:true, signed:true, url:'https://api.elections.kalshi.com/trade-api/v2/portfolio/balance'})}).then(r=>r.json()).then(console.log)
```

Should return account balance JSON.
